    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0419" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/766.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Kerens to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-07-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 50.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 36, of the
                    17th ultimo,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d287-f1"/> relative to participation of the
                    Austro-Hungarian Government in the Second International Opium Conference to be
                    held at The Hague, I have now the honor to transmit herewith a copy and a
                    translation of a personal note to me from Count Aehrenthal, minister for foreign
                    affairs, dated the 4th instant, from which it appears that the Austro-Hungarian
                    Government has decided finally not to participate in the said conference. I also
                    transmit a copy and a translation of the memorandum accompanying the minister’s
                    aforesaid note, giving the reasons for the nonparticipation of his Government,
                    but stating that it would follow with much interest the deliberations of the
                    conference.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. C. Kerens.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d287-a1.xml" xpointer="d287-a1"/>
